
same pane show in different windows?
	no tmux support except with nested tmux, should we nest everything?

borrowed per pane, the "parent" of the borrowed window is a pane, if the pane is move the borrowed stays attached to it
vs borrowed per window

borrow multiple in the current window/in its own window

putting utilities to sleep when not borrowed to save cpu

clone the borrowed utilities with a set the other panes, say that I have setup a layout with utilities for a project, shared utilities, clone the whole thing in another project space

registering a utility or a layout from the cli should add a template in the config or be a wizard using readline

--instance is only necessary when multiple instances exist and can't be differenciated by name, --fzf would list all the instances and allow multiple selections

if a utility needs arguments, query the argument automatically, a layout with multiple utilities needing arguments will ask for all the arguments for each utility; when savung a layout, user has the option to save the arguments or not

check that the tables in, all documents, once aligned do not break the 150 character width limit

